INT. MANOR LIBRARY - NIGHT

Leather spines. A cold hearth. A body-shaped chalk outline on the carpet beside a toppled globe. Rain on the leaded windows.

INSPECTOR GRIMSBY, 50s, rumpled, a pipe unlit in his teeth, circles the outline slowly while LADY ONDINE VANTERPOOL, 60s, in a black silk wrap, stands rigid by the fireplace, her cane planted like a flag, and FLORIAN AUBERT, 30s, the secretary, lingers in the doorway turning a pen over and over in his knuckles, and BRIDGET MULLANEY, 20s, the housemaid, hovers at a tray of cups, head bowed, eyes darting from one face to the next.

GRIMSBY
Lady Ondine, the clock.

ONDINE
What of it?

GRIMSBY
Stopped at ten past eleven.

ONDINE
It always stops.

FLORIAN
It's an old clock.

BRIDGET
My ma said it's cursed.

ONDINE
Bridget, hush.

BRIDGET
Sorry, ma'am.

GRIMSBY
Mr. Aubert, you were at the desk?

FLORIAN
All evening.

GRIMSBY
And you heard nothing?

FLORIAN
Not a thing.

ONDINE
He is deaf in the left ear.

FLORIAN
Slightly.

GRIMSBY
Convenient.

FLORIAN
It's a handicap, sir.

BRIDGET
He hears fine when the cook mentions pudding.

FLORIAN
Bridget!

ONDINE
Girl, to the kitchen.

BRIDGET
Yes, ma'am.

She doesn't move. Grimsby sets his pipe in the ashtray.

GRIMSBY
Stay, Miss Mullaney. You've something to say.

BRIDGET
I have not.

GRIMSBY
Then why the cups?

BRIDGET
What cups?

GRIMSBY
You've brought four. And there were five in the room.

Silence. Ondine's knuckles whiten on the cane. Florian's pen stops turning. Grimsby crosses to the globe, rights it, and spins it with one finger.

GRIMSBY (CONT'D)
The fifth cup was the dead man's. Someone took it. Someone with a reason.

ONDINE
Inspector, this is intolerable.

GRIMSBY
No, my lady. This is Tuesday.

Bridget lets out a tiny, strangled sound and sets down the tray. The cups rattle. She looks at Florian, who looks at the carpet. Ondine looks at neither.

GRIMSBY (CONT'D)
Miss Mullaney. Which of them told you to hide it?

BRIDGET
(whispering)
Nobody told me. I thought the cup was... it was warm. He was still warm.
